# auth.http — try every auth route from VS Code.
# Click "Send Request" above each ### block. Run them in order (1 → 12).
# Uses a clearly labeled DEMO account on example.com (a domain reserved for testing).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api

### 1. Health check (should say database: connected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Who am I? → 401 (not logged in yet)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 3. Register a DEMO user → 201 + Set-Cookie header
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mira.demo@example.com",
  "username": "mira_demo",
  "password": "tea under the willow",
  "birthDate": "1998-04-12",
  "agreeToGuidelines": true
}

### 4. Who am I? → 200 (the cookie from step 3 is sent automatically)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 5. Log out → 204
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout

### 6. Who am I? → 401 again
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 7. Log in → 200 (note the messy email: it gets cleaned)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "  Mira.Demo@Example.com ",
  "password": "tea under the willow"
}

### 8. Wrong password → 401 "That email and password don't match"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mira.demo@example.com",
  "password": "coffee on the moon"
}

### 9. Email that doesn't exist → 401 with the SAME message as step 8
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody.demo@example.com",
  "password": "coffee on the moon"
}

### 10. Same email again → 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mira.demo@example.com",
  "username": "another_mira",
  "password": "a different long phrase",
  "birthDate": "1998-04-12",
  "agreeToGuidelines": true
}

### 11. Under 18 → 400 with details.birthDate
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "teen.demo@example.com",
  "username": "teen_demo",
  "password": "a long enough phrase",
  "birthDate": "2015-06-01",
  "agreeToGuidelines": true
}

### 12. Sneaky "role": "admin" → 201, but the response shows role: "member" 🔒
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sneaky.demo@example.com",
  "username": "sneaky_demo",
  "password": "trying to be an admin",
  "birthDate": "1995-01-01",
  "agreeToGuidelines": true,
  "role": "admin"
}